Conventions search and tagging conventions
title end

paragraph start
Fuzzy search works on file names, so the area key comes right after the number and the last word names the kind of page.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The ending word tells you what the page is. Rules states what must always hold. Procedure gives ordered steps. Checklist is items to tick. Template is a skeleton to copy. List is a plain inventory. Register is a record of items that exist. Log is entries added over time. Plan is intended future work. Method describes how something is done. Recipe gives exact settings. Criteria are the tests for a choice. Profile describes one person or thing.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Each page also carries a tags line under its title, as the tag vocabulary page says.
paragraph end

